{"tool_name":"funomic","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"funomic","home":"https://github.com/ManichanhLab/FunOMIC","license":"Not licensed","summary":"Pipeline with built-in Fungal Taxonomic and Functional Databases for Human Mycobiome Profiling.","addition_date":"2022-09-16T23:47:13.071611Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:38:54.206556Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:funomic","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"cmanicha@gmail.com","name":"Chaysavanh Manichanh","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Zixuan Xie"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"DNA barcoding","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3200"},{"term":"Network analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3927"},{"term":"Taxonomic classification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3460"}]}],"name":"FunOMIC","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1016/j.csbj.2022.07.010","metadata":{"abstract":"While analysis of the bacterial microbiome has become routine, that of the fungal microbiome is still hampered by the lack of robust databases and bioinformatic pipelines. Here, we present FunOMIC, a pipeline with built-in taxonomic (1.6 million marker genes) and functional (3.4 million non-redundant fungal proteins) databases for the identification of fungi. Applied to more than 2,600 human metagenomic samples, the tool revealed fungal species associated with geography, body sites, and diseases. Correlation network analysis provided new insights into inter-kingdom interactions. With this pipeline and two of the most comprehensive fungal databases, we foresee a fast-growing resource for mycobiome studies.","authors":[{"name":"Manichanh C."},{"name":"Xie Z."}],"citationCount":7,"date":"2022-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Computational and Structural Biotechnology Journal","title":"FunOMIC: Pipeline with built